{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210732,"nonce":"rDXe8yisc/7d6pEho6SDXFOndYc=","title":"AOT-from-.hatch matched module_var_sources without normalising ./sibling","message":"Fixed in commit 9e7b48f. Record migrated from session memory 2026-09-12.\n\n\n`wlift --aot OUT bundle.hatch` produced a binary where `@hatch:web`'s\n`import \"./css\" for Stylesheet, Style, Css` left `Stylesheet`/`Style`/`Css`\nas null modvars. Surfaced as the hatch site hanging on every request:\n- TCP listener bound fine (\"@hatch:web listening on ...\").\n- TCP `accept` returned a conn.\n- The serve fiber never ran — `Scheduler_.new` saw null Scheduler_, so\n  `sched.spawn` silently mis-fired and `sched.tick` did nothing.\n\nSame source compiled directly from `.wren` (`wlift --aot OUT main.wren`)\nWORKED. The break was specific to the archive path.\n\n\n`compile_walk_to_object_with_manifest` matches each module's\n`module_var_sources[slot]` (the raw import string from source —\n`\"./css\"`) against earlier-emitted modules' `module_name` /\n`module_aliases`. Archive-bundled modules are stored under their\nMANIFEST name (`\"css\"`, normalized in `extract_archive_imports` via\n`normalize_archive_import_name`). The exact-string compare missed,\nso the binding fell through to RUNTIME — which also couldn't find\n`./css` in the registered modules. Net effect: target slot stayed\nzeroed.\n\nThe `.wren` walker doesn't have this problem because it uses the\nimport string verbatim as `request_name` when it recurses.\n\n\nNormalize `source_path` the same way the archive walker normalizes\nmanifest names, then try both spellings when matching:\n\n```rust\nlet source_path_normalized = normalize_archive_import_name(source_path);\nlet matched_idx = manifests.iter().take(idx).position(|src| {\n    \u0026src.module_name == source_path\n        || src.module_name == source_path_normalized\n        || src.module_aliases.iter().any(|a| a == source_path)\n        || src.module_aliases.iter().any(|a| a == \u0026source_path_normalized)\n});\n```\n\n\n- Hatch site (`hatch/site`) under AOT:\n  - `boot: catalog: 40 distinct packages loaded` (was null)\n  - `curl /healthz` → 200 OK `ok`\n  - `curl /` → 200 OK with the full landing-page HTML (~34KB)\n- Existing test corpus unchanged: 923 unit + 113 e2e + 21 aot_runtime;\n  proc 33/33, events 36/36, http 25/25, io 44/44, web 118/118.\n\n**Why:** Bundle storage keys (manifest names) and source-level import\nstrings have different normalization. Without unifying them at the\nbinding step, every `./sibling` import inside a bundled package\nsilently becomes a null modvar.\n\nWhen debugging \"AOT works from .wren but hangs from .hatch\", first\ncheck `WLIFT_AOT_DEBUG_IMPORTS=1` output for `RUNTIME` lines on\nrelative imports — those are the symptom. The fix above resolves the\nclass of bug for any future package that uses `./sibling` imports.","files":null}]}